{"name":"Lamiaceae","hex":"#3afddb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Lamiaceae","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic family within the order Lamiales – many plants related to mint, basil, and other such plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Lamiaceae"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lamiaceae","blocks":[{"text":"Lamiaceae or Labiatae is a family of flowering plants commonly known as mints, deadnettles, or sages. Many species in Lamiaceae are aromatic, and the family includes many widely used culinary herbs like basil, mint, rosemary, sage, savory, marjoram, oregano, hyssop, thyme, lemon balm, lavender, and perilla, as well as traditional medicines such as catnip, skullcap, bee balm, wild dagga, self-heal, and oriental motherwort."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Lamium_purpureum_jamestown1.jpg/330px-Lamium_purpureum_jamestown1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lamiaceae","wikidata":"Q53476"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Lamium_purpureum_Closeup.jpg/500px-Lamium_purpureum_Closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/01/Lamium_purpureum_Closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Lamium_purpureum_Closeup.jpg/500px-Lamium_purpureum_Closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALamium_purpureum_Closeup.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Leucas_aspera_at_Gandipet%2C_Hyderabad%2C_AP_W_IMG_9054.jpg/330px-Leucas_aspera_at_Gandipet%2C_Hyderabad%2C_AP_W_IMG_9054.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=t